From cdbff9ac647068465595a1667a8a8ae9f1e6d608 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 08:10:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v2.9.6: full-backup restore actually restores - drain the
 TLS-buffered upload tail

Every metal restore from v2.7.2 to v2.9.4 answered {"ok":0,"ek":"file",
"ec":"magic"} and did nothing. Two defects, both in our code, neither in the
stock tail:

1. do_reaper_restore_post gated each 1 KB fread() on select() of the RAW
   socket. Under TLS the last ~16-24 KB of the body sit in SSL_pending() +
   stdio buffers with the socket empty, so select() timed out and the loop
   broke with bytes still owed; the old `if (want > 0) goto out` threw them
   away. Stock do_upload_post has the identical loop but its post-loop slurp
   keeps writing to the fifo - our copy dropped the fputc. Mirror stock:
   drain from the FILE until the declared length is met, then judge short.

2. The card's stylesheet hides #rbk_msg / #rbk_pending with display:none;
   the injected JS un-hid them with style.display="" which only clears an
   INLINE style. Every message - and the v2.9.3 alert() fallback - was
   written into a div that stayed hidden. display="block" now.

Also: every refusal in both halves logs its stage / ek+ec to syslog (only
success logged before), do_upload_config stamps nvram-restored / committed /
reboot-requested, and the reply half waits up to 15 s for rc's /tmp/reboot
and re-requests once if it never appears.
